<VI _name="Car Wash Graft.vi" description="CAR WASH CONTROLLER - main VI.\0A\0ASimulates the control system of an automated car wash. The user selects the wash steps on the Entry Console\2C clicks Start\2C and moves the Car Position Slider to simulate the vehicle travelling through the wash. The controller drives the Car Wash Display\3A the Wash Entry LED\2C the eight wash step LEDs\2C the Vehicle Out of Position LED and the Elapsed Time indicator.\0A\0AARCHITECTURE - queue driven state machine\0AA single While Loop dequeues one state per iteration and executes the matching frame of the Case Structure; every frame decides which state runs next and enqueues it. The queue is the state store required by the specification\2C and its element type is an enumeration\2C so a new state is added by extending that enumeration and adding one frame - no other code changes.\0A\0AEach frame delegates its work to one subVI\2C so the main VI holds only the state machine skeleton and the front panel wiring.\0A\0ASTATES\0A  Initialize     - vacant\2C ready\3A all LEDs off\2C Elapsed Time 0\2C slider at Entry\2C Entry Console enabled. Entered at start-up and after every completed wash.\0A  Idle           - waits for Start.\0A  Configure Wash - turns the Wash Options selection into a step list\2C disables the Entry Console\2C sets Wash In Progress.\0A  Wash Step      - runs the active step\3A checks the vehicle position\2C accumulates the elapsed time\2C drives the LEDs.\0A  Wash Complete  - all steps done\3A Vehicle Out of Position lights as the exit prompt and the controller waits for the slider to reach Exit.\0A  Shutdown       - restores the vacant front panel state and stops the loop.\0A\0ARESPONSIVENESS\0AThe loop is paced by Wait (ms) at 50 ms\2C which is inside the 100 ms the specification allows and leaves the processor essentially idle.\0A\0ASTOP PROGRAM\0AThe stop button is read once per iteration outside the Case Structure and overrides the dequeued state with Shutdown\2C so the wash can be aborted in any state.\0A\0AREFERENCES\0AThe queue is released after the loop. The VI references the UI subVIs open are closed inside those subVIs.\0A\0ASlider scale\3A 0 = Entry\2C 1..3 = Station 1..3\2C 4 = Exit.">
